{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3ngVrUcRtgyLffrrcWc","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I committed the invoices export as `0b1ec08`. It's `scripts/export_invoices.py` plus its output, `out/invoices.csv`.\n\n**It filters out segment C, like the customers export.** The invoices table has no `seg` column, so copying the customers script as-is would have exported every invoice. The commit that added the segment filter (`007528c`) explains why it exists: segment C customers declined partner sharing, and \"nothing about them goes to the partner… every record we hold on them, not only this table.\" So the new script looks up which customer IDs are segment C in `tables/customers.csv` and drops their invoices.\n\n**What came out:** 8 of the 12 invoices, for customers 101, 102, 104 and 106. The 4 dropped invoices all belong to segment C customers. If you actually wanted every invoice exported, deleting the filter line in the script will do it.\n\nJanuary is still untouched: `data/2026-01.csv` is uncommitted and not included in this commit.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414,"cache_read_input_tokens":21158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":414,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-40>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:39.384Z","request_id":"gen-1794703474-siuCSjwQ8Y3p92xXPP4t"}
